From: NFC FeliCa Fix
Date: Fri, 4 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] akatsuki: Fix NFC FeliCa support for SO-01J DCM variant

The SO-01J (Docomo variant) uses Sony CXD224x FeliCa instead of NXP PN553.
This requires kernel configuration to use akatsuki_dcm config and proper
device tree overlay to enable FeliCa support.

LineageOS 22.2 was using generic akatsuki config (tama_akatsuki_defconfig)
which doesn't have proper FeliCa support, causing I/O errors and missing NFC toggle.

This patch changes kernel config to tama_akatsuki_dcm_defconfig which includes:
- CONFIG_MACH_SONY_AKATSUKI_DCM=y
- Proper device tree with FeliCa (CXD224x) configuration
- GPIO 63 pull-up for FeliCa interrupt (GPIO_FELICA_INT_N)
- Rohm BD7602 LDO driver support
- DTV tuner (MN88553) configuration for Docomo variant

Device tree changes include:
- &qupv3_se10_i2c with FeliCa at address 0x29
- FeliCa LDO (Rohm BD7602) at address 0x1e
- Proper GPIO configuration for FeliCa interrupt and wake lines

Change-Id: I0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567
---
 BoardConfig.mk | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/BoardConfig.mk b/BoardConfig.mk
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/BoardConfig.mk
+++ b/BoardConfig.mk
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ DEVICE_PATH := device/sony/akatsuki
 TARGET_SCREEN_DENSITY := 480
 
 # Kernel
-TARGET_KERNEL_CONFIG := tama_akatsuki_defconfig
+TARGET_KERNEL_CONFIG := tama_akatsuki_dcm_defconfig
 
 # HIDL
 DEVICE_MANIFEST_FILE += $(DEVICE_PATH)/manifest.xml
